    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability on the first attempt. The AddressSanitizer confirmed a stack-buffer-overflow in `INDEX_ORDERLY_RAM_Marshal` at `NVMarshal.c:4238` — exactly the line where `memcpy(&nrh, nrhp, sizeof(nrh.size))` reads 4 bytes past the end of the `indexOrderlyRam` buffer.\n\nThe exploit works by sending a single `TPM2_NV_DefineSpace` command that creates an orderly NV index with `dataSize=500`. Combined with the 12-byte `NV_RAM_HEADER`, this fills all 512 bytes of `s_indexOrderlyRam`, leaving no room for the 0-sized terminator entry. When the state is later marshalled, the loop in `INDEX_ORDERLY_RAM_Marshal` reads past the array boundary looking for the terminator that was never written.",
